{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"boundary","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A lost release response can leave the former owner's write window open after a successor acquires the lease, breaking the ownership boundary."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"resume","trigger":"plausible","reason":"After restart, restored active leases are omitted from renewal and can expire if the caller relies on the renewal loop without reacquiring."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An unapplied pending acquisition after a network failure causes a later run to be refused without reconciling the available claim."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"test","trigger":"normal","reason":"The mutant test cases pass because they change the assertions, leaving the requested invariant demonstration missing without establishing a runtime defect."}]}